# Get started

This site is a [PokeDocs](https://wbaxterh.github.io/pokedocs/) site:
diagram-native, branded from one config block, and readable by both humans
and AI agents.

## Run it

```bash
npm install
npx playwright install chromium   # once — renders diagrams at build time
npm run start
```

`npm run build` produces the deployable static site in `build/`.

## Add a page

Create a Markdown file under `docs/` with a `description` in its
frontmatter — the sidebar picks it up automatically:

```md
---
sidebar_position: 3
description: One sentence agents and search results will see.
---

# My new page
```

See [Authoring](./authoring.md) for the full conventions, and `AGENTS.md`
at the repo root if an AI agent writes docs alongside you.

## Make it yours

Everything brand-specific lives in `docusaurus.config.ts`:

- `branding.brandColor` — the whole color theme, both light and dark
  modes, is derived from this one value.
- `customFields.landing.cards` — the cards on the landing page.
- `url` / `baseUrl` — set these when you know where the site deploys.
